# The Quiet Archive - EP12 The Great Library of Alexandria (an evening around 230 BC, under Ptolemy III)
# Structure: for the first time the thread is an object, not a person or a walk. We follow one scroll - a copy of the
#   popular star poem of Aratus, the Phaenomena - from the moment it arrives on a merchant ship from Rhodes at dusk,
#   through the city and the garden of the Muses, onto a copyist's desk, into the catalogue and the shelves, and finally
#   up onto a flat roof where an old scholar reads it under the very stars it describes. Order: the harbour and the
#   lighthouse -> the harbour office -> the Canopic Way -> the garden of the Muses -> how a book is made -> the copyists
#   -> the tables of Callimachus and the shelves -> the measurer of the world -> stars over the harbour (goodnight).
# New scenes: "pharos" = the Great Harbour at dusk: the three-tiered lighthouse (square, octagonal, round, statue on
#   top) on its island with the fire burning and a slow plume of smoke (_pharosfire), the long Heptastadion causeway,
#   the fire's light trembling on the water (_wlights) and a single-masted merchant ship with a square sail and a swan-
#   neck stern gliding in to harbour (_galley).
# "rooftop" = a flat Alexandrian roof at night: parapet with water jars and a potted palm, a bronze bowl sundial
#   (scaphe) and a gnomon, the white city of flat roofs below, the colonnades of the Canopic Way with lamps, the Pharos
#   fire far away (glowspot), stars brighter than usual with a few constellations of Aratus slowly twinkling.
# "mouseion" = the garden of the Muses: a colonnaded walk (peripatos) in perspective with lamps, a long pool with the
#   moon in it (reflect), date palms whose fronds sway (_palms), the curved stone seat of the exedra, a scholar walking
#   slowly along the colonnade (_walker).
# "scriptorium" = the copyists' room: lamps on stands (_lamps), a long table, a seated copyist whose reed pen moves
#   along the line (_scribe), scrolls on the table, ink pots, a papyrus sheet drying, a window with a palm and the moon.
# "stacks" = a long hall of wooden pigeonholes in one-point perspective, each holding rolled scrolls with little title
#   tags that stir in the night air (_tags), a lamp-bearer far down the hall.
# New "motes" particles (tiny gold flecks drifting slowly up through lamplight); palette keys "lime" and "papyrus".
